  "coverage": "Counted from the 1,833 stocks in the daily scoring run (the run checked 1,838 stocks for 2026-11-04 and scored 1,833; 5 had too little data to score and are not counted); 1,498 of the scored stocks have a sector on record and 335 do not; of the ones with a sector, 1,487 traded on 2026-11-04 with the 21 sessions behind them and are counted in the averages, and 11 did not trade that session and are not counted; the 335 names with no sector on record are listed by name on this page as unmapped, with the reason",
  "definitions": {
    "average": "A sector's figure is the average of its counted stocks' price changes over the window: each counted stock's closing price on the last session in the price history, compared with its closing price 5 (or 21) of its own trading sessions earlier. Every counted stock counts once, whatever its size, and the number counted is printed beside the figure.",
    "leading_lagging": "A sector that is not turning and ranks in the top three over 21 sessions is leading; one that is not turning and ranks in the bottom three over 21 sessions is lagging; any other sector is in the middle.",
    "thin": "A sector with fewer than 10 counted stocks is too thin to rank: it is named as thin and shows its counts only, with no average and no label.",
    "turning": "A sector is turning when its average change over the last 5 sessions points the opposite way from its average change over the last 21 sessions: rising lately after falling over the longer stretch, or falling lately after rising.",
    "universe": "The count covers the stocks in the daily scoring run, which are stocks listed today, so stocks that stopped trading earlier are not in it."
  },
